Z||000000||Jericko||08-13-2001||07:58 PM||||I have an 84 Fiero SE, 4 cyl the 2.5L I believe, anyways just put a new starter in it, and have a battery with 14 Volts, I believe.  Sometimes I cant start my car, I get a click from the starter but there is no ignition, if I wait about 30 minutes or so, and beat the hell out of my starter, it may start.  I've thought that maybe my starter is stuck in "engage position" so I've tried rolling it about ten-fifteen feet and dropping it into gear (it is an auto) then try to start it, this worked the first time but does not seem to really work now, any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||86seyellow||08-13-2001||08:35 PM||||dude, <P>tiem to cough up soem ash for your car and spoil her with a starter. I cant believe you new this was going on for a while and didnt take care of yoru car sooner. <BR><P>------------------<BR>if you saw a yellow streak go by you really fast it was a fiero<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-13-2001||08:45 PM||||If it clicks when you try to start it sometimes, I would think that it would be a Low battery.But you said it sometimes starts back up after about 30 min of beating the starter.Not sure but I would now be inclined to think you have a faulty starter. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||08-14-2001||03:00 PM||||Sounds like a bad spot in one of the windings.  Beating on it gets it just past the bad spot.  Also you did not say if this is a old start or hot start.  That does make a diffrence.  My question is why would you think to beat on it???????????  I have never had to "beat" any part of my car to make it work......but hey thats just me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroMaster88||08-14-2001||04:03 PM||||I am gonna have to go with bad starter.   I had a 86 SE with the 2.5 and it was an auto.  When it was warm I had to wait 30 to 60 min for it to start again...the starter would just click.  Changed the starter and the problem went away.<P>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
